#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""S180 close — splice the S180 entry into MISSION-CONTROL.md and roll S174
to the archive (newest-first), keeping ~6 live entries."""
import io, re, shutil

MC = 'MISSION-CONTROL.md'
AR = 'MISSION-CONTROL-ARCHIVE.md'

ENTRY = """### Session 180 — 2026-07-20 — TWO CROSS-PAGE TEMPLATES BROKEN (84 headings + a 7-page shared closing machine), the multiplied-close queue 48 → 15 / severe 1 → 0, all eight §C debts PAID, and 70 hyperlinks stripped out of quoted Scripture

**§A — THE SEVEN-PAGE CLOSING MACHINE (the find of the session).** Seven pages closed with the identical six-part device: `"So we confess it, who once ___:"` → a tricolon of *that*-clauses → `"We did not A; He B."` → `"To the Father who…, to the Son who…, to the Spirit who…"` → `"be all the glory of every ___"` → `Amen.` → a bolded stinger. Two of the italic closing quotations were near-verbatim across pages (*"Even my faith was Yours. The whole way, it was Yours."* / *"It was You. The whole way, it was You."*). The seven cross-link to each other, so a reader on an ordinary path met the same machine three times in an hour — VOICE §XVIII.3 and §XXII.5 in their purest form. **All seven closes rewritten from scratch**, each riding its own page's native image and each at a deliberately different temperature: apologetic-bought-with-his-own-blood (plain, no stinger; new ground — *a price reveals what the buyer would spend, not what the object was worth*, which corrects the "you're worth the blood of Jesus" sentimentality that quietly makes the sinner the valuable thing) · apologetic-darkened-in-their-understanding (still, short — *"Genesis does not record the void's consent"*) · apologetic-loved-darkness-rather-than-light (hot; also repaired a conditional-comfort stinger, now *"The light never waited to be wanted"*) · apologetic-purchased-from-every-tribe (lyrical, the note of joy — *"You were bought into the choir"*) · systematic-faith (cool; faith as the glass you look **through**, never at — kills the introspection loop the page's own penultimate paragraph flirted with) · systematic-perseverance (the quietest close on the site, no stinger — the childhood dark bedroom seen again in daylight) · systematic-repentance (*"No one turns in an empty room"*). Machine residue site-wide: **0**.

**§A — the individually-confirmed defects.** question-external-call re-landed its own beat near-verbatim (*"You needed both. And God provided both."* … *"You needed both. He provided both."*) — first instance trimmed, the Circular Return kept as the true destination. question-whose-side-are-you-on asked its title question twice, the second time **after** the paragraph answering it; the mid-page form also handed the reader the deciding vote (*"Which side do you want to be on?"* → *"Two accounts of how you got here. Only one of them is true."*). **question-is-predestination-in-the-bible ended on a guardrail failure** — *"The only question is whether you will believe it."* — the final sentence of a page arguing faith is a gift returning the deciding vote to the reader; rewritten to end on the doctrine enacting itself. Its *"No serious biblical scholar… denies"* (an unsourced evaluative authority claim, §XXII.4) replaced with the countable record: **proorizō, six occurrences — Acts 4:28, Rom 8:29, 8:30, 1 Cor 2:7, Eph 1:5, 1:11.** Four after-the-Amen re-opens repaired (devotional-cold-church's post-prayer callout was *also* a feeling-slip that read the reader's ache as evidence and shamed anyone feeling nothing; demolition-works-righteousness's nav rail moved above its prayer so a demolition ends in the catch; anxious-mind-the-loop's hammer folded into its landing).

**A CONSECRATED / BORN-APEX PAGE CARRIED THREE BANNED MOVES.** invisible-wall-prayer-feels-empty: crisis-triage / search-intent rhetoric (*"You found this page by searching for something you were embarrassed to type"*, *"Remember the search bar?"*, *"a page you almost didn't click"*), the odd-hour crisis frame (*"at an hour when no one else was awake"*), and the feeling-slip twice (In Brief: *"the very ache to pray is itself the quiet evidence that grace still has hold of you"*). Its real opener — the bedroom, the clasped hands, the words falling to the carpet like stones — was universal, excellent, and buried under the funnel paragraph. The Circular Return now returns to **that**, which makes the original hammer *"Someone was."* land harder because it answers the page's own scene. **A site-wide sweep found only one other case** (question-are-arminians-saved), also fixed. *No label exempts — proven again.*

**§B — THE SIXTH AND SEVENTH CROSS-PAGE TEMPLATES BROKEN: 84 headings rewritten in one pass.** `<h2>The Steel Man — …>` on **64** pages and `<h2>The Socratic Trap…>` on **20**, six of the latter carrying the *identical* heading, "Three Questions the Arminian Cannot Answer." Both are labels naming a **move** where a heading should be doing work (§I.3: H2s are sentences, not labels) — and a heading that names the technique is the checklist showing through the paint (§XVIII.3). Most pages already carried the objection in the reader's own voice right after the label, so stripping the label left a genuinely varied set; **23 that were flat category labels were hand-written from each page's own argument** ("The Multiverse" → *"With Enough Universes, One of Them Had to Look Like This"*; "of the Counter-Move" ×2 → *"Paul Chose a Church, Not a List of Names"* / *"The Past Tense Is a Pattern, Not a Promise"*; the six identical Socratic headings → *"Whose Hand Is on the Leash?"*, *"What Is Verse 9 Doing in the Paragraph?"*, *"On What Basis Does a Nation Become a Soul?"*, etc.). Two collided after stripping ("But People Do Fall Away" on both apologetic-kept-by-the-power-of-god and systematic-perseverance) and were de-collided. The camp label went too: "Three Questions the *Arminian* Cannot Answer" both names a party where Scripture should be named and taunts, which §XIX forbids. Residue: **0** headings; remaining mentions are `<meta name="keywords">` only.

**§C — ALL EIGHT DEBTS PAID.** **demolition-children-of-satan** never named *prevenient grace*: its trilemma treated "From God?" as automatically yielding election when the able Arminian's answer **is** "from God." Wesley's position now stated at full strength in his own terms and answered on the one point it cannot carry — identical grace in two men, one believes, so the deciding factor is supplied by the man; 1 Cor 4:7 closes it, and the non-resistance reply ("an omission is not a contribution") is closed in the same pass per §XXII.1.6. **question-dead-man-visual** told and did not show: a concrete §XIII.3 mirror added — **the enemy-love test**, new to the §XIII.2 bench (*try to want good for the person you like least; you can produce the intention, you cannot produce the wanting*), which the reader can run in ten seconds and cannot fake; its *"The Greek is grammatically airtight"* now names the word (*dynamai*, negated: *ou dynatai*), the *"this is the crown-jewel argument"* editorial-jargon leak is gone, and Ezek 36:26's link to `/question-ezekiel37` is repointed to `/question-newheart`. **systematic-christology**: the premature pullquote needed no relocation — the identical sentence already closes the *tetelestai* paragraph where it lands, so the early copy was deleted; the embodied-cognition overclaim ("three decades proving", leaning on the warmth/insula version — Williams & Bargh 2008 is a landmark failed replication) rebuilt on semantic somatotopy (Hauk et al. 2004), with the limit stated aloud. **secular-neuroscience-human-inability**: Soon et al. now carries its accuracy figure (**~60% against a 50% baseline**) — the honest number is the *better* argument, since a faint early bias ten seconds out is exactly what the doctrine predicts and mind-reading is not; "Neuroscience has demonstrated five things" restated at the strength the data support, with the concession made explicitly. **devotional-in-christ** "fourteen verses" → twelve. **question-ephesians1**: "the longest sentence in the New Testament" (hero + meta + OG + JSON-LD, five places) hedged to "among the longest" to match the body, and "well over two hundred words" → "roughly two hundred."

**NEW SYSTEMIC FIND — 70 HYPERLINKS WERE SITTING INSIDE QUOTED SCRIPTURE AND HEADINGS.** The auto-linker's guard (S177/S178) stops new injections; **nobody ever swept the damage already on disk.** 50 links inside `scripture-quote` / `verse-block` / `verse` containers and 20 inside `<h1>`–`<h4>`, across **26 pages**. This is not cosmetic: the site quotes the NIV verbatim with no "(NIV)" suffix precisely so a reader can open his own Bible against ours, and a gold hyperlink inside the verse makes part of the quotation read as editorial emphasis — the text we ask him to trust as untouched has visibly been touched (§V.2 + §IX.4). All 70 `<a>` wrappers removed, inner text preserved, so no word of any verse changed. Every real article held 13+ prose links; the five pages now under the floor are all non-prose utilities (objection-builder, printable-five-points, reformed-sources, the-60-second-case, verse-navigator), which CLAUDE.md exempts.

**TOOLING — `detect-multiplied-close.js`: two more false-positive classes found and killed, plus a new positional check.** **(4) INTERACTIVE-WIDGET CHROME** — the-fork.html topped the queue at **9** (the only severe entry) on nothing but UI: its `<div class="fork-actions">` button rails wrap only `<button>`/`<a>`, so the S179 container-div rule misses them and the `<a>` is too small a fraction of the text for the link-only rule. `fork-actions|fork-btn|fork-progress|fork-stage|next-step` added to FURNITURE. **(5) THE TWO-BEAT PAGE IS THE PRESCRIBED SHAPE** — one catch + one hammer scored **6** on the doxology bonus alone, which is what put ~10 `apologetic-*` pages in the queue on a clean ending; the bonus now requires an actual stack (3+ beats). **NEW: the after-the-Amen flag (`!`).** A hammer, stinger or callout printed past a prayer re-starts a page the reader had been released from. Weighted **+1**, not more, and deliberately: one short line after a prayer can be legitimate (the prayer is the reader's; the last line is God's word back over him) — it is a defect when mechanical, when it restates the prayer, or when it belongs to a shared formula. The flag also had to be tightened to require a closing "Amen": the DOXOLOGY regex fires on doxological *prose* and over-fired on 30 pages before that. **Queue: 48 multiplied / 1 severe → 15 multiplied / 0 severe. Structural rot held at 0 (secondary 216 → 156).**

**Pipeline** GREEN. Deviations from baseline: search-index **687** · mega-menu **657** · homepage-counts **609** · **auto-linker 1** (verified safe, then the 70-link legacy sweep run after it) · wire-orphans 0 orphans / 76 unmapped · canonical **1** (the known benign matt23-37 stub) · verify-scripture 3831 quotes / DIVERGENT 273 / "(NIV)" **0** · rot **0**. **`validate-site.js` CHECK 7 earned its keep on its first live run** — it caught `scripture-audit-report.txt` (regenerated at the repo root by `verify-scripture.js` every session) as newly publicly-servable and printed the exact rule; added, now **95 forced rules**.

**Carries forward (S181):** the remaining **15** multiplied closes (all 6–8, no severe) · the 27 after-the-Amen `!` pages for a hand-check pass, most of which are legitimate · **"doctrine of election" on 23 pages** (CLAUDE.md prefers "doctrines of grace"; needs per-instance judgement, one is a legitimate `compare-*` taxonomy use) · re-home the links stripped from Scripture into the prose gloss beside each verse · §E deferred items. **§XIX ledger — SPENT THIS SESSION: 1 Cor 4:7 ("who makes you different from anyone else?") on the prevenient-grace trilemma.** Still unspent: **Matt 5:45**. **New to the §XIII.2 bench: the enemy-love mirror.** **New to the watched-image ledger: the window/glass ("look through, never at"), the childhood dark bedroom, the empty room a turn requires.**

---

"""

s = io.open(MC, encoding='utf-8').read()
anchor = '### Session 179 — 2026-07-20'
assert s.count(anchor) == 1
shutil.copy(MC, 'archive/s180-backup/MISSION-CONTROL.md')

# roll S174 to the archive (newest-first)
m174 = re.search(r'### Session 174 —.*?(?=\n### Session 173 —|\Z)', s, re.S)
assert m174, 'S174 block not found'
block = m174.group(0)
s = s.replace(block, '', 1)

a = io.open(AR, encoding='utf-8').read()
hdr = re.search(r'^(#[^\n]*\n(?:>[^\n]*\n|\n)*)', a)
a = a[:hdr.end()] + '\n' + block.rstrip() + '\n\n---\n\n' + a[hdr.end():]
io.open(AR, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(a)

s = s.replace(anchor, ENTRY + anchor, 1)
io.open(MC, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)

live = re.findall(r'### Session (\d+) —', io.open(MC, encoding='utf-8').read())
print('S180 spliced. S174 rolled to archive.')
print('live entries now:', live)
